From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:35:40 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0400): sidecar IPC endpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fork side of the RemoteSmith fork<->sidecar IPC, protocol v1 (docs/IPC.md;
DEF-4, DEF-17, DEC-5, §6.2, §6.2a, §6.3; AC-20, AC-21, AC-25, AC-55, AC-60).

- src/remotesmith/: protocol types ported verbatim from the sidecar, the
  endpoint (hello/negotiation, bounded lines, malformed-input handling,
  client cap, write and hello deadlines, per-topic pushes, MAX_LINE on
  output), snapshot collectors (saved peers, LAN + rendezvous presence,
  macOS TCC/launchd/pmset/fdesetup and Windows service/powercfg/BitLocker
  readiness, registration, key fingerprint, cold-boot ledger), connect via
  the existing `--connect` path with no credential on the IPC.
- macOS: listens in the per-user server process at
  /tmp/<AppName>-<uid>/remotesmith-ipc.sock (0700 dir, 0600 socket, peer
  uid check); never in a root process.
- Windows: the --tray process (user token) creates
  \\.\pipe\<AppName>-ipc-<user> with a user-only DACL and relays sessions,
  registration and BitLocker state from the SYSTEM --server through the new
  ipc::Data::RemoteSmithHost request.
- Everything runs on its own threads and runtime; RustDesk never waits on it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
